      "title": "obex: Use consistent L2CAP CID for packet look up",
      "message": "obex: Use consistent L2CAP CID for packet look up\n\nBT L2CAP connections have two channel identifiers (i.e. CIDs), one for\neach endpoint of the connection. The CID in an L2CAP packet is the\nendpoint that the packet is directed toward. Hence, for an L2CAP\nconnection, sent/received packets will most likely have different CIDs.\n\nWhen the OBEX dissector encounters a request packet using L2CAP as the\ntransport, it stores the packet in a wmem_tree using the L2CAP CID for\nthe \"channel\" key. When the dissector receives the corresponding\nresponse packet, it attempts to retrieve the request packet using the\nresponse packet's L2CAP CID. Since the request and response packets most\nlikely don't use the same CID, looking up the request packet in the\nwmem_tree can lead to retrieving the wrong packet. When this issue\noccurs, the response packet can be dissected incorrectly. The request\npackets also don't have their response frames set.\n\nChange the \"channel\" key for L2CAP OBEX packets to use the L2CAP\n\"local CID\", which is consistent for all packets in an L2CAP connection.\n",
